d by OMIM, Mar 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q969S0","text":"Antiporter that transports nucleotide sugars across the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane in exchange for another nucleotide sugar. May couple UDP-alpha-D-glucuronate (UDP-GlcA) or UDP-alpha-D-xylose (UDP-Xyl) efflux to UDP-alpha-D-glucuronate (UDP-GlcA) influx into the ER lumen, which in turn stimulates glucuronidation and excretion of endobiotics and xenobiotics. [Isoform 1]: Has UDP-GlcA:UDP-GlcNAc antiporter activity. [Isoform 2]: Has UDP-GlcA:UDP-GlcNAc antiporter activity."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}